# INFORMATOR PP (staff scraper)
# Captcha-verified session cookie. How to get it:
# open https://informator.put.poznan.pl/app/employees in a browser,
# then DevTools (F12) -> Application -> Cookies -> copy the 'informator' cookie value.
INFORMATOR_SESSION=null

# =============================================================================
# LLM
# =============================================================================
# Two models are configured independently and share one API key:
#
#   OPENAI_*  the agent that answers questions
#   JUDGE_*   the judge that scores evaluation runs
#
# Keep them on DIFFERENT models. A judge sharing the generator's weights shares
# its blind spots: the model that invented a room number is the least likely to
# flag that invention. Ingestion needs no key at all.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TEMPERATURE AND REASONING ARE MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE — BLANK MEANS "DON'T SEND IT"
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The two settings belong to two different kinds of model, and no model takes
# both:
#
#   REASONING MODELS do not accept `temperature` through the API at all. The
#   API rejects it as an unsupported parameter — it is not clamped, ignored or
#   warned about. What you steer instead is `reasoning_effort`: how much the
#   model thinks before answering.
#
#   PLAIN CHAT MODELS are the reverse. They accept `temperature` (how random
#   the sampling is, usually 0.0-2.0) and know nothing about `reasoning_effort`
#   — sending it is likewise an API error.
#
# So for each of the two models below, fill in EXACTLY ONE of its temperature /
# reasoning_effort and leave the other blank. Blank omits the parameter from
# the request entirely, instead of sending an empty string or a zero.
#
#   kind       example models   temperature      reasoning_effort
#   ---------  ---------------  ---------------  --------------------------
#   reasoning  GPT-6, GPT-5.6   not accepted     none|low|medium|high|xhigh|max
#   chat       GPT-4.1          0.0 - 2.0        not accepted
#
# A typo in reasoning_effort (or a non-numeric temperature) is rejected at
# startup with a readable message, rather than surfacing as an API error
# partway through an evaluation run.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY THE AGENT'S REASONING EFFORT IS PINNED TO "none"
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The agent calls tools. Per OpenAI's docs, Chat Completions supports function
# calling on the GPT-6 family ONLY at reasoning_effort=none, so any other value
# breaks tool use — and without tools the bot has no data and invents answers.
# That is why it is set rather than left blank, and why it is the one value to
# revisit when changing OPENAI_MODEL.
#
# The judge has no such limit: it uses structured output, not function calling,
# so JUDGE_REASONING_EFFORT may be anything. Blank takes the model default
# (whatever the model's own default is). Raising it costs two judge calls per gold-set
# case, so
# measure whether it changes any verdict before paying for it.


# API key from https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# --- agent (answers questions; uses function calling) ---
OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-6-luna
OPENAI_TEMPERATURE=
OPENAI_REASONING_EFFORT=none

# --- judge (scores eval runs; uses structured output) ---
JUDGE_MODEL=gpt-6-sol
JUDGE_TEMPERATURE=
JUDGE_REASONING_EFFORT=
